From 13c192737efbc20686e8e66315fac37f0f9553c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 06:35:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 66/98] libm: genuine 80-bit long double (mathl.c + long-double
 complex)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the cast-through-double long-double math with native x87
computations, fixing both the ~11-bit precision loss and — more
importantly — the exponent-range truncation that made any in-range
long double above DBL_MAX overflow to inf before computing.

mathl.c / math_wrap.c (x87 instructions used):
- exp/log: expl/exp2l/exp10l/expm1l (f2xm1+fscale, Cody-Waite reduction),
  logl/log2l/log10l (fyl2x), log1pl/log2p1l/log10p1l (fyl2xp1)
- trig/inverse: sinl/cosl/tanl/sincosl (fsin/fcos/fsincos/fptan + fprem1
  reduction), atanl/atan2l/asinl/acosl (fpatan + fsqrt, full domain checks)
- roots/power: sqrtl (fsqrt), cbrtl (fxtract + long-double Newton), hypotl
  (magnitude-factored, no naive x^2+y^2), powl (fyl2x+f2xm1+fscale, full
  C99 F.9.4.4 table), powrl/pownl/rootnl/compoundl/rsqrtl
- hyperbolic: sinhl/coshl/tanhl/asinhl/acoshl/atanhl in long double
- rounding: rintl/nearbyintl/floorl/ceill/truncl/roundl (frndint),
  lrintl/llrintl/lroundl/llroundl
- manipulation: frexpl/ilogbl/logbl/copysignl/scalbnl/ldexpl/modfl and
  crucially nextafterl/nexttowardl — true 80-bit mantissa stepping (the
  whole point of nexttowardl), never via double
- fmodl/remainderl/remquol (fprem/fprem1), fmal, fmin/fmax/fdim family

Long-double complex (cmath_explog/hyper/trig.c): cexpl/clogl/csqrtl/cpowl,
csinhl/ccoshl/ctanhl/casinhl/cacoshl/catanhl, ccosl/csinl/ctanl/casinl/
cacosl/catanl, cabsl/cargl — reimplemented in long double on the now-80-bit
scalars, keeping the double versions' special-value/branch-cut behavior.

Verified vs the host's 80-bit libm: expl(11000)=1.735e4777 (finite, was
inf), hypotl(1e2000)=1.414e2000 (was inf), nexttowardl ULP=1.08e-19 (was
the double 2.2e-16), complex variants to 0 rel error, transcendentals
within ~16 ULP.  Depends on the preceding __fpclassifyl fix.

Still double-based (no x87 primitive; noted in source, a later pass):
erfl/erfcl/tgammal/lgammal(_r), the Bessel jNl/yNl, and the complex
special functions clgammal/ctgammal/cerfl/cj0l... .

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
